questions.prompt:
The recursive function below alters the standard binary search base case from `start > end` to `start >= end`. All four choices search `[-67, -13, 22, 33, 60]`. Which call is the ONLY one that returns an incorrect result?

```python
def buggy_bsearch(numList, start, end, item):
    if start >= end:
        return -1
    middle = (end + start) // 2
    if numList[middle] == item:
        return middle
    elif numList[middle] > item:
        return buggy_bsearch(numList, start, middle - 1, item)
    else:
        return buggy_bsearch(numList, middle + 1, end, item)
```

